---
import { workflow } from '../data/site';
---
<div class="workflow-v11" aria-label="Multi-model AI research workflow">
  <div class="workflow-source">
    <span class="workflow-source-dot"></span>
    <div>
      <strong>Research question / repository</strong>
      <small>Scientific intent + current codebase</small>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="workflow-pipeline">
    {workflow.map((step, index) => (
      <>
        <div class={`workflow-step ${step.kind === 'gate' ? 'workflow-step-gate' : ''} ${step.kind === 'human' ? 'workflow-step-human' : ''}`}>
          <div class="workflow-step-top">
            <span class="workflow-step-index">0{index + 1}</span>
            <span class="workflow-step-kind">{step.kind}</span>
          </div>
          <strong>{step.name}</strong>
          <em>{step.role}</em>
          <p>{step.note}</p>
          <div class="workflow-output">{step.output}</div>
        </div>
        {index < workflow.length - 1 && <div class="workflow-connector" aria-hidden="true"><span>→</span></div>}
      </>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="workflow-verification">
    <div>
      <span class="verification-badge">Verification gate</span>
      <strong>Reconnaissance is evidence, not implementation authority.</strong>
    </div>
    <p>Critical claims are checked against the live repository before Codex edits code. If the report and repository disagree, the repository wins and the discrepancy is surfaced.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="workflow-footnote">
    <span>Copilot → IDE assistance</span>
    <span>Kiro CLI → CLI agents</span>
    <span>MCP → GitHub / Notion / Drive / Gmail</span>
    <span>Human-in-the-loop → scientific QC</span>
  </div>
</div>
